{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Quickly goes.</b> From the root of צועים, and צעוהו (Jeremiah 48:12). Behold, צועה is like 'sits in siege and straits,' and if it is a standing participle, the meaning is like 'bound,' and the word להפתח is for 'to the opening.'" "<b>And he shall not die to the pit.</b> This is the prophet." "<b>And he shall not lack his bread.</b> Like Micaiah (I Kings 22:27) and Jeremiah (Jeremiah 37), that they fed him bread of affliction."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:01.423501004Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}